{
 "_doc": "Cloud Search's model catalogue (Chat > Search > the model chip): the curated SELECTION, one row per provider per section, Anthropic first as the reference and then the best open-weights model of each provider. Which model, its params and its licence are written here by hand because OpenRouter does not publish them; a value marked *_est is an estimate, not an official figure, and the page says \"est.\". Prices are NOT authored here: the app reads them live from the OpenRouter catalogues in `urls` at most once every refresh_hours, caches them on the phone and ranks each section by them. `snapshot` is the bundled offline fallback, read from those catalogues on pricing_as_of; the page shows that date whenever it is what is on screen. Every id is checked against the live catalogues by test-keyboard-ai-routing.sh T9 (the AI model registry gate) and against the recorded fixture by core ModelCatalogueTest.",
 "_doc_fields": "section.kind: chat (selectable for the chat) | embeddings | rerank | audio | image (browsable, greyed: not a chat model). section.catalog: which OpenRouter catalogue prices the rows: chat (/models) | embeddings (/embeddings/models) | images (/images/models, priced per endpoint) | videos | none. A row whose id is not in the images catalogue is looked up in the videos one. rank_by: output | input - the price a section is ranked by (input for embeddings, where output is not billed). snapshot.unit: tokens ($ per 1M) | image | megapixel | second.",
 "version": 1,
 "pricing_as_of": "2026-10-10",
 "refresh_hours": 24,
 "urls": {
  "chat": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models",
  "embeddings": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/embeddings/models",
  "images": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images/models",
  "videos": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/videos/models",
  "model_endpoints": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models/{id}/endpoints",
  "image_endpoints": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images/models/{id}/endpoints"
 },
